# دائرة الانتظار والإشعار

The loading indicator is named **دائرة الانتظار** (`#appRing`). It sits in the center of the screen, fills, then disappears. Show it only when a request is actually slow, or immediately when the user picks an agent to log in as. Do not add a seconds counter, and do not disable the activation submit button.

System messages use **one** corner toast (`.sas-toast`):

- **ALL temporary notices** (success/error/info, sync, activate, transfer, save…): fixed at the **TOP** of the screen (desktop and phone), horizontally centered, then **slide UP and fade** after ~3 seconds. Never place temporary toasts at the bottom, middle of the page, or floating over content.
- Sticky notices (close button, no auto-hide): same top placement — subscription ended, account suspended, and SAS-offline. Do not show the same notice twice.
- Do not also render the same message as an inline `.alert`.
- Toast z-index must stay above modals (e.g. 100050). Always move the toast node to `document.body` via `placeCornerToast`.
